{"id":"389a25d3cf383a61","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-thm-kolmogorov-extension.md","title":"Kolmogorov Extension Theorem","display":"thm-kolmogorov-extension — Kolmogorov Extension Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-kolmogorov-extension","aliases":["58-thm-kolmogorov-extension","Kolmogorov Extension Theorem"],"display":"thm-kolmogorov-extension — Kolmogorov Extension Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch09/58-df-product-measure.md]]","[[58-df-probability-space.md]]","[[58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-kolmogorov-extension"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-kolmogorov-extension</span><span>Kolmogorov Extension Theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-kolmogorov-extension — Kolmogorov Extension Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"18ad6e37d70b294d\" href=\"?note=18ad6e37d70b294d\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-product-measure.md\">../batch09/58-df-product-measure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"58-df-probability-space.md\">58-df-probability-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"2bc25b4a67d5fe1e\" href=\"?note=2bc25b4a67d5fe1e\" title=\"58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space.md\">58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> (index set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(E_t,\\mathcal E_t)_{t\\in T}\">\\((E_t,\\mathcal E_t)_{t\\in T}\\)</span> (family of standard Borel spaces)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\">\\(\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\)</span> (nonempty finite subsets of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu_J\">\\(\\mu_J\\)</span> (probability measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\prod_{t\\in J}E_t\">\\(\\prod_{t\\in J}E_t\\)</span> for each <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"J\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\">\\(J\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi_{K,J}:\\prod_{t\\in K}E_t\\to\\prod_{t\\in J}E_t\">\\(\\pi_{K,J}:\\prod_{t\\in K}E_t\\to\\prod_{t\\in J}E_t\\)</span> (coordinate projection for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"J\\subseteq K\">\\(J\\subseteq K\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S\\)</span> (probability-measure and standard-Borel predicates)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kolmogorov\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\Bigl(\\forall t\\in T\\;\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S(E_t,\\mathcal E_t)\\land\\forall J\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\;\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\bigl(\\mu_J,\\prod_{t\\in J}E_t,\\bigotimes_{t\\in J}\\mathcal E_t\\bigr)\\land\\forall J,K\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\;(J\\subseteq K\\to(\\pi_{K,J})_*\\mu_K=\\mu_J)\\Bigr)\\to\\exists!\\mathbb P\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\bigl(\\mathbb P,\\prod_{t\\in T}E_t,\\bigotimes_{t\\in T}\\mathcal E_t\\bigr)\\land\\forall J\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\;((\\pi_{T,J})_*\\mathbb P=\\mu_J)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kolmogorov\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\Bigl(\\forall t\\in T\\;\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S(E_t,\\mathcal E_t)\\land\\forall J\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\;\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\bigl(\\mu_J,\\prod_{t\\in J}E_t,\\bigotimes_{t\\in J}\\mathcal E_t\\bigr)\\land\\forall J,K\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\;(J\\subseteq K\\to(\\pi_{K,J})_*\\mu_K=\\mu_J)\\Bigr)\\to\\exists!\\mathbb P\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\bigl(\\mathbb P,\\prod_{t\\in T}E_t,\\bigotimes_{t\\in T}\\mathcal E_t\\bigr)\\land\\forall J\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\;((\\pi_{T,J})_*\\mathbb P=\\mu_J)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Kolmogorov: a projectively consistent family of finite-dimensional laws on standard Borel state spaces extends uniquely to the product <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-algebra.</li>\n<li>Every finite-dimensional marginal is now explicitly required to be a probability measure; projective consistency alone does not supply normalization or countable additivity.</li>\n<li>Foundation of probability theory on product spaces</li>\n<li>Cylinder sets generate the product sigma-algebra</li>\n<li>Existence of Brownian motion and Poisson processes</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Billingsley, Probability and Measure</li>\n<li>Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch09/58-df-product-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"18ad6e37d70b294d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-product-measure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-probability-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-probability-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"2bc25b4a67d5fe1e","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"(E_t,\\mathcal E_t)_{t\\in T}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu_J","display":false},{"tex":"\\prod_{t\\in J}E_t","display":false},{"tex":"J\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi_{K,J}:\\prod_{t\\in K}E_t\\to\\prod_{t\\in J}E_t","display":false},{"tex":"J\\subseteq K","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kolmogorov\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\Bigl(\\forall t\\in T\\;\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S(E_t,\\mathcal E_t)\\land\\forall J\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\;\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\bigl(\\mu_J,\\prod_{t\\in J}E_t,\\bigotimes_{t\\in J}\\mathcal E_t\\bigr)\\land\\forall J,K\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\;(J\\subseteq K\\to(\\pi_{K,J})_*\\mu_K=\\mu_J)\\Bigr)\\to\\exists!\\mathbb P\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\bigl(\\mathbb P,\\prod_{t\\in T}E_t,\\bigotimes_{t\\in T}\\mathcal E_t\\bigr)\\land\\forall J\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{fin}}^+(T)\\;((\\pi_{T,J})_*\\mathbb P=\\mu_J)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\sigma","display":false}],"bytes":2158,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4255","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-thm-kolmogorov-extension.md|58-thm-kolmogorov-extension]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["18ad6e37d70b294d","0578a357a86e9d8f","2bc25b4a67d5fe1e"]}